  "notes": "Adam and Hawwa are never drawn (named in text only); growth for the spreading of mankind (no people), a house for the ties of kinship, coins for the orphans' wealth. 2:4-7 is not glossed: the tafsirs read «الخبيث بالطيب» differently. STAGING v4: 1: mankind is addressed (1:1-2): an uncountable crowd of men and women in a town bows on 1:3 and 1:18 (fear of their Lord); a second crowd appears on 1:13 (spread over the earth, growth plate ended before the Name); they speak on 1:21 (asking one another by Him) and the second crowd walks to the first on 1:23 (ties of kinship, house plate ended before the Name). Adam and Hawwa are never drawn. 2: at home, a guardian hands a purse to the grown orphan on 2:1 (Al-Muyassar: when they reach puberty and can keep their wealth), who raises his hands; the prohibitions (2:4-12) are not acted, only the camera moves. No child figure."
